  "notes": "USAGE:\n{貸与|たいよ}する is the formal counterpart of {貸|か}す. It is commonly used in business, government, and educational contexts where lending is official or documented.\n\nASPECT (ている):\n{貸与|たいよ}されている indicates that the item is currently on loan.\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- [thing]を{貸与|たいよ}する (to lend something)\n- [person]に{貸与|たいよ}する (to lend to someone)\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {貸与|たいよ}{品|ひん} (loaned item)\n- {貸与|たいよ}{型|がた}{奨学金|しょうがくきん} (loan-type scholarship)\n- {無償|むしょう}{貸与|たいよ} (free loan)\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n{貸|か}す is the everyday word for lending. {貸与|たいよ}する implies a formal, institutional loan.",
